{
  "description": "Speaker-background layer wire contract, Qendresa item 16 extension (`full_screen_windows`, capability `speakerFrameWindows`, protocol 41). Inside a full-screen window the speaker's own take is drawn full-frame and untouched: no person mask, no background (fill, colour or window) and no `speaker_frame`; everything else (cutaways, cards, text) draws as usual. Outside every full-screen window the layer renders exactly as v2/v3 say. Windows are sorted by `start`, never overlap (touching ends are fine), last at least 0.5 s, end within 1800 s, and number 1...4. Every `valid` layer must decode (Python SpeakerBackgroundLayer, Swift SpeakerBackgroundLayer) and equal its `normalized` form; every `invalid` entry must be rejected by both. v1.json, v2.json and v3.json still apply unchanged: a layer without the key serialises exactly as there. `full_screen_windows: null` is read as absent on both sides and never written; `[]` is invalid.",
